WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.157 --> 00:00:14.445
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What are you doing in the UK?

2
00:00:14.952 --> 00:00:18.602
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> In the UK, er, I just came for a visit.

3
00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:25.589
I’m here the second time in my life, and it was always a dream of mine to come to London.

4
00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:28.000
Er, yes.

5
00:00:28.786 --> 00:00:33.205
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Was there anything that surprised you about the UK when you arrived?

6
00:00:33.991 --> 00:00:42.008
<v><b>Anna:</b></v> I think that the people are very open, and that, um, just everybody is so nice,

7
00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:48.576
and I also saw some monuments and some places I wanted to see,

8
00:00:48.698 --> 00:00:52.628
so I was also very impressed about the architecture, etc.

9
00:00:59.126 --> 00:01:01.781
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How do people in your country drive?

10
00:01:02.471 --> 00:01:03.885
<v><b>Madeleine:</b></v> I think it depends where you are.

11
00:01:03.903 --> 00:01:08.418
Where I live in Oregon, everything is very safe, much slower, but in New York City

12
00:01:08.418 --> 00:01:12.034
everything is very fast, very dangerous.

13
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:15.597
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Are you a typical driver for where you live?

14
00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.283
<v><b>Madeleine:</b></v> I would say so, I d-, I’m a very cautious driver.

15
00:01:25.396 --> 00:01:28.470
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have any ambitions for this year?

16
00:01:29.117 --> 00:01:33.116
<v><b>Chris:</b></v> Um, yes, I’d like to visit my daughter in Australia,

17
00:01:33.151 --> 00:01:36.068
and also plan towards my retirement.

18
00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:39.981
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you think you’re going to do them?

19
00:01:40.907 --> 00:01:45.693
<v><b>Chris:</b></v> Certainly the planning, whether or not I achieve the visit is something else.

20
00:01:51.527 --> 00:01:54.776
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Have you ever seen a film more than three times?

21
00:01:54.968 --> 00:01:58.863
<v><b>Talitha:</b></v> Yes, I really like <i>Lord of the Rings</i>, so I’ve definitely seen that more than three times.

22
00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:00.802
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you like about it?

23
00:02:01.247 --> 00:02:03.867
<v><b>Talitha:</b></v> I love the scenery, um,

24
00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.199
and I love the imagination.

25
00:02:11.963 --> 00:02:13.745
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What phone do you have?

26
00:02:14.059 --> 00:02:15.456
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I have an iPhone.

27
00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:16.871
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How old is it?

28
00:02:17.063 --> 00:02:21.063
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I believe, I believe my iPhone is now two years old.

29
00:02:22.531 --> 00:02:24.836
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> How often do you change phones?

30
00:02:24.906 --> 00:02:27.544
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> Um, I change phones maybe every three years.

31
00:02:28.661 --> 00:02:30.801
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What do you use it for the most?

32
00:02:31.002 --> 00:02:33.220
<v><b>Martin:</b></v> I mostly use my phone for social media.